  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Slapjack. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Slapjack (or 'Slaps') is a children's card game that tests speed and reflexes. Players take turns flipping cards onto a central pile. When a Jack appears, the first player to slap the pile wins all the cards in the center. The goal is to collect the entire deck.",
    objective: 'Collect the entire deck by winning the center pile when a Jack is played. The first player to slap the center pile when a Jack appears wins the pile and adds it to the bottom of their face-down stack.',
    gameplay: 'The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Turn your card so all players see it at once; do not peek in advance.',
      'Only Jacks are slapped; first to slap the pile wins it.',
      'False slap: give your top card to the player who played the wrongly-slapped card.',
      'Run out of cards: one more chance to slap a Jack to re-enter; otherwise you are out.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two to eight players; sources recommend about 4–10 for best play. Each player holds their cards as a face-down pile and takes turns flipping to a center pile. Play proceeds clockwise.',
      deck: 'One standard 52-card French deck. The pack is divided roughly equally between all players; everyone holds their cards as a face-down pile. No jokers or extra cards are used.',
      equipment: 'Standard playing cards, table.',
      dealing: 'Deal entirely to players face-down into personal piles.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'The pack is divided roughly equally between players; each holds cards as a face-down pile. Going clockwise, each player places the top card of their pile face up in the centre. When a Jack is played, the first player to slap the pile wins the centre pile and adds it face down to the bottom of their pile; play continues from the left of the winner. Do not peek at your card before turning it; everyone must see it at once. False slap: if you slap when the top card is not a Jack, you give your top card to the player who played that card. If you run out of cards, you may still slap the next Jack to re-enter; if you fail or false-slap, you are out. The player who has all the cards wins.',
